# Changelog

All notable changes to this project are documented here.

## [2.0.0] - 2026-08-10

Behaviour of eight exports changed, so this is a major release. Every change below is a fix for
something that was wrong, but code depending on the old output will see different results — read
"Breaking" before upgrading.

### Breaking

- `getDelta` — returned a negative number, and with the default `size = 0` always returned
  `-|a - b|`. A distance is now non-negative. With a positive `size` the two numbers sit on a
  wrapping space and the shorter way around is returned, never more than `size / 2`.
- `getMapDistance` — arguments reached `getDelta` in the wrong order (`(size, Xa, Xb)` against a
  `(a, b, size)` signature), so the map size was mixed into a coordinate. The distance between
  (40,70) and (50,50) returned `417.73`; it is now `22.36`.
- `getOverlapRange` — two ranges sharing a start or an end were an overlap in one argument order
  and not in the other: `getOverlapRange(0, 2, 0, 1)` gave `[0, 1]` while `getOverlapRange(0, 1, 0, 2)`
  gave `[0, 0]`. The result is now the intersection and does not depend on argument order. Ranges
  that merely touch are still not an overlap.
- `toFormData` — nesting deeper than two levels lost every ancestor above the innermost:
  `{a:{b:{c:1}}}` posted as `b[c]` instead of `a[b][c]`, so two sibling branches with the same
  inner shape collided on one key. The bracket chain now carries the full path.
- `timeToSeconds` — returned `NaN` when called with no argument, despite defaulting to an empty
  string. Absent and blank components now count as zero. A component that is present but not a
  number still yields `NaN`, so malformed input stays visible.
- `formatNodeList` — an `HTMLCollection`, which the signature accepts, was wrapped as a single
  element instead of being expanded, producing a one-item array holding the collection itself.
- `isJson` — its declared return type `Record<string, T> | false` did not match its behaviour,
  which returned any parsed JSON value. It now accepts only objects and arrays, returns `false`
  for a bare value, and is typed `Record<string, T> | T[] | false`. This also removes an
  ambiguity: `isJson('false')` parsed to the same `false` used to signal failure. Use `getJson`
  when any JSON value is acceptable.
- `getJson` and `isJson` no longer write to `console.error` on invalid input. A malformed string
  is expected input for both and the return value is the report; the logging was noise the caller
  could not switch off.

### Added

- `ISecondsToTimeMap` and `ISetCookieOptions` are exported from the package root. They were
  reachable only by importing the emitted declaration file directly.
- `exports` map in `package.json`, with a `types` condition so the published types resolve under
  `moduleResolution: node16` and `bundler`.
- Property-based tests (fast-check) over the pure functions, covering round trips, idempotence,
  symmetry, the triangle inequality and per-input bounds. The `getOverlapRange` asymmetry above
  came from one of its counterexamples, now committed as a named regression case.
- Type-level tests (expect-type) over the exported signatures, gated by `tsc` — `isolatedModules`
  puts ts-jest in transpile-only mode, so a type error in a test never fails a jest run.
- Packaging smoke test (`npm run test:pack`): packs a tarball, installs it, imports it as both
  CommonJS and ESM, calls a real function and type-checks the published types.
- Per-file mutation baseline (`mutation-baseline.json`) with a gate that fails a file dropping
  below its recorded score and raises the baseline when one improves.
- `README.md` documenting the whole API, and `TESTING.md` documenting the test layers.
- CI jobs for the packaging test and the mutation baseline.

### Changed

- `npm run build` cleans `dist/` first. Six modules whose sources had been removed
  (`arrayDivide`, `matrixTranspose`, `prefersDarkScheme`, `prefersReducedMotion`, `sort`,
  `whitelist`) were still being published.
- `npm run typecheck` now type-checks the test tree as well as `src`.
- `tsconfig.json` includes `dom.iterable`, which `getForm`, `getIndex` and `appendChildren`
  already relied on.

### Fixed

- Three pre-existing type errors in the test suite, invisible until the tests were type-checked.
- `formatNodeList`'s empty-input test asserted nothing: jest's `toEqual` treats `[undefined]` as
  equal to `[]`.

## [1.2.3] - 2026-08-05

### Fixed

- `toFormData` — a plain `Blob` was silently dropped instead of being appended. The recursion
  guard tested `instanceof File`, so any binary value that was not a `File` (`canvas.toBlob()`,
  `fetch().blob()`, most image croppers) took the recursive branch; a `Blob` has no enumerable
  own properties, so nothing was appended and the upload went out with no file and no error.
  The guard now tests `instanceof Blob`, which covers `File` too since `File` extends `Blob`.

## [1.2.2] - 2026-07-28

### Added

- `getExecTime` — time a sync or async function's execution, resolving with its result and elapsed milliseconds
- `deleteFile` — delete a file, resolving `true`/`false` on success/absence, with an optional `onError` callback for unexpected failures
- `coerceStringArray` — coerce any value (array, comma-separated string, single value, `null`/`undefined`) into a trimmed `string[]`

## [1.2.1] - 2026-07-23

### Changed

- Hardened the test suite via mutation testing (Stryker), raising the overall mutation score from ~75% to ~90% with every source file now at or above 70%
- `secondsToTime` — removed a redundant always-true guard inside the loop and iterate with `Object.entries` (no behavior change)

## [1.2.0] - 2026-07-20

### Added

- `getUrlQueries` / `setUrlQueries` — parse and build URL query strings, framework-agnostic (works standalone or alongside any router)
- `copyToClipboard` — copy text to the clipboard, with an `execCommand` fallback for older/insecure contexts
- `downloadBlob` — trigger a client-side file download from a `Blob` or raw content
- `isInViewport` — check if an element is (fully or partially) within the viewport
- `getCookie` / `setCookie` / `deleteCookie` — read, write and remove cookies
- `prefersReducedMotion` / `prefersDarkScheme` — `matchMedia` convenience wrappers

### Removed

- `arrayDivide` — duplicate of lodash's `chunk`
- `matrixTranspose` — duplicate of lodash's `zip`
- `sort` — duplicate of lodash's `orderBy`
- `whitelist` — duplicate of lodash's `pick`
